    [Cherry-pick][main][CI][Docker] Update pinned dependency build dates for v0.30.0 (from #19532) (#19535)
    
    Cherry-pick of PR #19532 onto `main`.
    
    Original PR: #19532
    Original author: @czydyy
    
    ---
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Update the pinned daily build dates across the v0.30.0 Dockerfile
    variants:
    - memcache and memfabric: `20261022.5` (where installed)
    - torch-npu: `20261015.5`
    
    Keep `MEMCACHE_DATE` and `MEMFABRIC_DATE` defined separately so the
    package URLs resolve correctly.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. Images built from these Dockerfiles use the updated dependency
    builds.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - `git diff --check` passed.
    - Verified each Dockerfile that installs memcache and memfabric defines
    `MEMCACHE_DATE`, `MEMFABRIC_DATE`, and `TORCH_NPU_DATE` exactly once.
    - Pre-commit codespell, typos, filename, and sign-off checks passed.
    - Docker images and NPU tests were not run locally. The gitleaks and
    symbolic-meta pre-commit hooks could not run on this Windows host
    because `/bin/bash` and Python are unavailable; the commit was created
    with `--no-verify`.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/a98247ab4db686ee03c66d5feb3c761e52a2f8ab
    
    Co-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>

